    "n4": `Read or transmit your YouTube comments, search history, watch history, or account information`,
    "n5": `Use advertising SDKs, third-party analytics, or behavioral tracking`,
    "n6": `Access your microphone, camera, clipboard, or downloads`,
    "n7": `Inject ads into the YouTube page itself — the overlay only shows a small rank badge that you can disable`,
    "n8": `Sync any of your data to our servers`,
    "n9": `Require an account, login, or email to use the extension's core features`,
    "s6_p1": `YT Radar is compliant with the Brazilian Lei Geral de Proteção de Dados (LGPD) and the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), and compatible with CCPA.`,
    "s6_h3a": `Rights you have`,
    "r1": `<strong>Access</strong> — All local data is visible via <code>chrome://extensions</code> → YT Radar → Inspect views → Application → Storage`,
    "r2": `<strong>Deletion</strong> — Removing the extension automatically clears all <code>chrome.storage.local</code> data. You can also clear it manually in your browser settings`,
    "r3": `<strong>Promotion data</strong> — If you submitted a Community Spotlight item, you can manage or delete it using the access token displayed on the success screen of the submission form. Lost the token? Contact us with the email used at submission`,
    "r4": `<strong>Opt-out</strong> — Set Overlay to "Off" in Settings to disable the in-page overlay. Closing the popup stops all extension network activity`,
    "s6_h3b": `Legal basis for processing`,
    "s6_p2": `Top 50 fetches and video detail lookups are processed under <strong>legitimate interest</strong> (delivering the feature you opened the extension for). Spotlight promotion submissions are processed under <strong>contract performance</strong> with the submitting creator. No other processing occurs.`,
    "s7_p1": `For privacy questions, data deletion requests, or promotion management:`,
